Do not fclose a NULL log file: the destructor segfaulted at every shutdown of the robot.
fopen(Log/pos_log.txt) fails when Log/ is not writable (ROOT_DIR is the build-time source tree, root-owned in the image; the stack runs as a normal user),
so `fp` stays NULL and `fclose(fp)` in ~LaserMappingNode crashes: exit code -11 on every SIGTERM/SIGINT (the gn_supervisor restart, Ctrl-C).
Measured on the Nano: 6/6 exits 139 as a user, 0/12 as root, 6/6 clean as a user with a writable Log/ mounted.
Base: hku-mars/FAST_LIO a4743b0 (ROS2 branch) + 0001 + 0002.

diff --git a/src/laserMapping.cpp b/src/laserMapping.cpp
index d5f450b..8085856 100644
--- a/src/laserMapping.cpp
+++ b/src/laserMapping.cpp
@@ -944,7 +944,7 @@ public:
     {
         fout_out.close();
         fout_pre.close();
-        fclose(fp);
+        if (fp) fclose(fp);   // NULL when Log/ is not writable (the image's is root's, the robot runs as a user): fclose(NULL) segfaults at every shutdown
     }
 
 private:
